#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0143 expect=violation domain=DS
#note "W5 (PLAN-grouped-aggregate-functions phase 0, scenarios first): the rule had no scenario. min_date(DSSTDTC, domain=\"DS\", group=[USUBJID]) is the earliest DSSTDTC over ALL of the subject's DS rows (no DSDECOD filter, unlike CG0068), and the Check fires on the informed-consent row only when that row IS the earliest and DM.RFICDTC differs from it. P1: the earliest DS row is the consent row (2026-01-01, a later consent copy on 01-05) and RFICDTC is 2026-03-15 -> fires on row 1 only. P2: consent row is the earliest and RFICDTC equals it -> quiet. P3: a RANDOMIZED row precedes the consent row, so the consent row is not the earliest -> quiet even though RFICDTC differs (the rule's own 'possible underreporting'). Written and run on the pre-port engine (cumba-corej@8513690): GREEN before, pins what stands."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=P1 DSSTDTC=2026-01-01
dataset DS label=Disposition
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ type=Num label="Sequence Number"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | P1 | 1 | INFORMED CONSENT OBTAINED | 2026-01-01
S1 | DS | P1 | 2 | INFORMED CONSENT OBTAINED | 2026-01-05
S1 | DS | P2 | 1 | INFORMED CONSENT OBTAINED | 2026-01-01
S1 | DS | P2 | 2 | RANDOMIZED                | 2026-01-10
S1 | DS | P3 | 1 | RANDOMIZED                | 2025-12-20
S1 | DS | P3 | 2 | INFORMED CONSENT OBTAINED | 2026-01-01
---

dataset DM label=Demographics
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col RFICDTC type=Char label="Date/Time of Informed Consent"
---
S1 | DM | P1 | 2026-03-15
S1 | DM | P2 | 2026-01-01
S1 | DM | P3 | 2026-03-15
---
